#: ../../../internals/ethdebug_internal_debug_info.rst:11
msgid ""
"ethdebug support and the interchange format described here are experimental. "
"They may change before ethdebug output is stabilized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../internals/ethdebug_internal_debug_info.rst:16
msgid ""
"This page is an initial draft and is deliberately kept out of the "
"documentation TOC. It still mixes user-facing material with compiler "
"internals; the two will later be split into separate documents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../internals/ethdebug_internal_debug_info.rst:19
msgid ""
"The compiler emits public debug info using the `ethdebug format <https://"
"github.com/ethdebug/format>`_. This page describes the internal debug info "
"passed from the Solidity frontend through Yul before the public resources "
"and contexts are emitted. At a textual compiler boundary, the debug info is "
"a JSON sidecar paired with the Yul source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../internals/ethdebug_internal_debug_info.rst:25
msgid "Terminology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../internals/ethdebug_internal_debug_info.rst:27
msgid ""
"Several established terms are ambiguous in this context, so this page pairs "
"each with a more specific replacement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../internals/ethdebug_internal_debug_info.rst:29
msgid ""
"*Metadata* elsewhere means the contract metadata embedded in bytecode. Data "
"intended for debuggers is therefore called *debug info* on this page, never "
"metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../internals/ethdebug_internal_debug_info.rst:31
msgid ""
"*Location* elsewhere names both positions in source text and the data "
"locations of the Solidity language such as storage, memory, and calldata. "
"This page uses *source range* for bytes in Solidity or Yul source text and a "
"pointer's *region location* for EVM data in stack, storage, transient "
"storage, memory, calldata, returndata, or code; the two are unrelated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../internals/ethdebug_internal_debug_info.rst:33
msgid ""
"*Pointer* elsewhere often means a Solidity storage or memory reference. "
"Unless qualified that way, *pointer* on this page means an `ethdebug pointer "
"<https://github.com/ethdebug/format/blob/main/schemas/pointer.schema.yaml>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../internals/ethdebug_internal_debug_info.rst:36
msgid ""
"Fields introduced by this format follow these terms, for example "
"``declarationSourceRange``. Existing compiler structures keep their "
"established names, for example ``SourceLocation`` and the ``nativeLocation`` "
"and ``originLocation`` fields of ``DebugData``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../internals/ethdebug_internal_debug_info.rst:41
msgid ""
"The first implementation stage is intentionally narrower than the format "
"specified here. It will leave variable updates empty, emit public variable "
"contexts only for storage-backed variables, and not yet cover immutable, "
"constant, or other variables whose materialized representation is not "
"storage-backed. Yul optimization with ethdebug is also deferred. These are "
"implementation staging limits, not sidecar-format constraints."
msgstr ""

